# I/O traceability logging

Every user-facing LLM flow **must** log inputs and outputs for auditability.

## What to log

On each estimation (and similar LLM endpoints):

| Side | Fields |
|---|---|
| User input | `request_id`, endpoint, `description` (full text), enums, `prompt_version` |
| Model output | `request_id`, `provider`, `model`, `estimation` (full text), token counts if available |
| Failures | `request_id`, error class/message (no API keys) |
| Prompt render | `prompt_version`, `prompt_hash` (from the Jinja loader) |

Use **structlog** (`app.logging_config`) and a shared `request_id` across the request.

## Rules

- Log **before** the LLM call (input) and **after** success (output)
- On provider errors, log the failure with the same `request_id`
- **Never** log API keys, raw `.env`, or Authorization headers
- Prefer structured events: `logger.info("event.name", field=value, ...)`
- OpenAPI `json_schema_extra` / `examples` are **docs only** — they are not runtime responses and must not replace tracing

## Do not

- Rely on Swagger examples as proof of what was returned
- Skip logging because the payload is large (truncate only if explicitly required later)
- Log secrets or provider credentials
